<div><h1>Comparing concepts across time</h1><p class="sub">Six comparative questions, twelve controlled-to-historical studies</p></div>
</section>

<main class="reading">
<p class="lede">Every module opens with one created, controlled study before it turns to real artworks from different places and periods. <span>Within a module, the controlled study always comes before its historical exploration — a small rule marks that shift, not a claim that one kind of evidence supersedes the other.</span></p>
<p class="page-note">The controlled comparison images are original studies made with OpenAI GPT Image 2 through Codex, built to model one visual relation at a time — they are teaching illustrations, not historical evidence. Historical artworks are separately identified and credited where they appear.</p>

